.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt OSSL_STORE-WINSTORE 7ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm OSSL_STORE-winstore
.Nd OpenSSL built in OSSL_STORE for Windows
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The OSSL_STORE implementation for Windows provides access to Windows'
system
.Qo Li ROOT Qc
certificate store through URIs, using the URI scheme
.Qo Li org.openssl.winstore Qc .
.Ss Supported URIs
There is only one supported URI:
.Bd -literal
  org.openssl.winstore:
.Ed
.Pp
No authority (host, etc), no path, no query, no fragment.
.Ss Supported OSSL_STORE_SEARCH operations
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xr OSSL_STORE_SEARCH_by_name 3
As a matter of fact, this must be used.
It is not possible to enumerate all available certificates in the store.
.El
.Ss Windows certificate store features
Apart from diverse constraints present in the certificates themselves,
the Windows certificate store also has the ability to associate
additional constraining properties alongside a certificate in the store.
This includes both documented and undocumented capabilities:
.Bl -bullet
.It
The documented capability to override EKU
.It
The undocumented capability to add name constraints
.It
The undocumented capability to override the certificate expiry date
.El
.Pp
.Em Such constraints are not checked by this OSSL_STORE implementation, and thereby not honoured .
.Pp
However, once extracted with
.Xr OSSL_STORE_load 3 ,
certificates that have constraints in their X.509 extensions will go
through the usual constraint checks when used by OpenSSL, and are
thereby honoured.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ossl_store 7 ,
.Xr OSSL_STORE_open_ex 3 ,
.Xr OSSL_STORE_SEARCH 3
.Sh HISTORY
The winstore
.Pf ( Qo Li org.openssl.winstore Qc )
implementation was added in OpenSSL 3.2.0.
.Sh NOTES
OpenSSL uses
.Xr OSSL_DECODER 3
implementations under the hood.
To influence what
.Xr OSSL_DECODER 3
implementations are used, it's advisable to use
.Xr OSSL_STORE_open_ex 3
and set the
.Em propq
argument.
